      "created_at": "2013-05-08T17:59:02.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I just noticed when looking at the box mock-up on Kickstarter how much stonework there is on GSF components. &nbsp;The backgrounds on Station cards are stone with a chisel emboss. &nbsp;The box has the same stone background/emboss. &nbsp;It's an unusual choice for a space game, where you don't typically see a lot of stonework in space. &nbsp;You'd normally expect to see more glass and steel on boxes and components. Maybe this was part of the obviousness of the fantasy theme? &nbsp;Or maybe stone backgrounds is just not the best choice for a space game? &nbsp;Any thoughts?</p>",
